1. Combat System
Inputs:
Left Click – Light Attack
Right Click – Heavy Attack
Space – Dodge
F – Parry
Weapons:
Daggers: Fast, short range. 8–15 damage.
Swords: Balanced speed and range. 10–20 damage.
Greatswords: Slow, high damage. 18–30 damage.
Spears: Long range, moderate damage. 10–18 damage.
Rules and Numbers:
Players have 100 stamina, regenerating 15 per second.
Attacks consume 5–30 stamina depending on the weapon.
Dodging costs 15 stamina and provides 0.3 seconds of invincibility.
Parrying costs 10 stamina and staggers enemies for 1.5 seconds.
2. Weapon Mastery System
Input: Uses combat controls.
Rules and Numbers:
Defeating enemies grants 5 mastery XP for the equipped weapon.
At 25 XP, players unlock a new combo.
At 50 XP, players unlock a special attack costing 30 stamina.
Each weapon has its own mastery progression.
How They Interact:
Combat allows players to fight using different weapons, while Weapon Mastery rewards continued use by unlocking new attacks and combos.
Then, for each of your mechanics, one sentence on which of your others it changes and how.
Combat System → Evan’s Enemies: Different weapon types, attacks, dodges, and parries change how players fight enemies, allowing them to deal damage, avoid attacks, and stagger enemies.
Weapon Mastery System → Evan’s Enemies: Unlocking new combos at 25 XP and special attacks at 50 XP gives players additional ways to fight enemies and bosses, changing how combat encounters play out.
